WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.660
Signals matter in C because they introduce asynchronous control flow.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:15.320
A process may be reading a file, updating shared state, holding a lock, writing a log entry, waiting for a child process, or preparing a shutdown path when a signal is delivered.

3
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.780
The handler does not wait for the program to reach a tidy checkpoint.

4
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.840
It may run at a moment that ordinary program logic did not expect.

5
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:29.160
That timing makes signal handling a reliability and security engineering concern.

6
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:37.420
A handler that performs complex work can interfere with resource state, cleanup behavior, logging, and shutdown decisions.

7
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:45.520
Even a program that works well during routine testing may behave differently when interruption happens during initialization, during an update, or during a failure path.

8
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:51.400
The safest mental model is to treat signal paths as part of the trusted control design.

9
00:00:51.500 --> 00:01:00.620
Developers should know which signals the program handles, what each handler is allowed to do, what state the handler can touch, and how the handler communicates with normal code.

10
00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.080
If those answers are unclear, the program is depending on timing assumptions that are hard to review.

11
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.680
Signals are not only about termination.

12
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:20.300
They can be involved in child process notification, configuration reload requests, terminal events, timers, operational supervision, and crash-related diagnostics.

13
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:27.040
Each use should have a narrow purpose and a documented flow from asynchronous notification to safe mainline processing.

14
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.840
Throughout this course, the goal is practical discipline.

15
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:41.660
Keep handlers small, make shutdown deliberate, avoid complex behavior inside asynchronous context, and verify that cleanup works when interruption happens at awkward times.

16
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.560
Secure signal handling is less about clever code and more about predictable control flow.
